      "message": "We don\u0027t need to check response_size \u003c FLASH_PAGE_SIZE here:\n\nNull-termination is not required: printf(\"%.*s\", (int)response_size, response) specifies an explicit precision. It prints at most response_size bytes and stops early only if it hits a \\0, so it does not need a terminating null character even when the buffer is completely filled (response_size \u003d\u003d FLASH_PAGE_SIZE).\n\nBuffer capacity is already enforced: response_size is initialized to sizeof(response) (equal to FLASH_PAGE_SIZE) before the call and passed by pointer to send_vendor_command(), which treats it as the maximum buffer capacity. Both the TPM path (MIN(len, *response_size)) and the USB path clamp the received size so response_size can never exceed FLASH_PAGE_SIZE.\n\nEnd-of-log detection: If the question was whether \u003c FLASH_PAGE_SIZE indicates the last chunk of log data, the loop in main() calls get_console_logs() repeatedly until the GSC returns an empty response (response_size \u003d\u003d 0).",
